16
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,820
So let's find out what happens,

17
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:26,260
step by step,

18
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,700
starting with the very first second.

19
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:31,960
The moon is about 384 ,000

20
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:32,840
kilometers away.

21
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,160
Its light takes about 1 .3

22
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,380
seconds to reach you,

23
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,140
so for just over a second,

24
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,620
you would still see it.

25
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:40,300
Then,

26
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,460
the sky goes dark where it

27
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:43,160
used to shine.

28
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,780
On the night side of Earth,

29
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,740
millions of people look up at

30
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:47,120
once.

31
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:48,380
Phones come out,

32
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:50,020
the internet explodes,

33
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:52,400
scientists rush to their telescopes,

34
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:54,580
but the real changes are only

35
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:55,400
just beginning.

36
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:56,260
First,

37
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:57,960
the night gets darker,

38
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,220
much darker.

39
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,040
A full moon can light up

40
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:01,920
a whole field.

41
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:02,940
Without it,

42
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,800
every night is like a moonless

43
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:05,100
night.

44
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:06,100
In the city,

45
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,560
you might barely notice,

46
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,940
but in the countryside,

47
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:11,000
nights become pitch black.

48
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,220
And for animals,

49
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:13,640
this is a big deal.

50
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:15,000
Some night hunters,

51
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,060
like owls,

52
