66
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:37,360
straight line.

67
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,240
But there is one good side.

68
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:40,480
Without moonlight,

69
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,740
the stars shine brighter than ever.

70
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:43,940
The next morning,

71
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:46,100
something strange happens at the beach.

72
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:48,360
The tide barely moves.

73
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,360
That's because the moon is the

74
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,840
main reason we have tides.

75
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:54,420
Its gravity pulls on Earth's oceans,

76
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,720
making them bulge.

77
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:57,960
As Earth spins through that bulge,

78
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,900
