79
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:01,780
The sun makes tides too,

80
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,840
but they are smaller.

81
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,080
Without the moon,

82
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,980
tides would shrink to about a

83
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:06,220
third.

84
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,860
Gentle ripples instead of big highs

85
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:09,420
and lows.

86
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,940
That changes everything for life on

87
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:12,380
the shore.

88
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,420
Tide pools are home to crabs,

89
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:15,280
starfish,

90
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:15,980
and snails.

91
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:18,100
They depend on water coming in

92
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,640
and going out every day.

93
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,860
With weak tides,

94
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:22,600
many of these places would dry

95
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,640
out or change.

96
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:24,700
Mudflats,

97
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:26,400
where millions of birds feed,

98
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,240
could shrink.

99
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,400
Tides also mix the ocean,

100
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:31,140
stirring up nutrients.

101
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:33,500
Weaker tides mean calmer,

102
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,860
less mixed water near the coast.

103
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:38,300
Fishermen who plan around the tides

104
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,580
would need new rules.

105
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:42,040
Some harbors built for big tides

106
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,700
might suddenly feel shallow.

107
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,060
Tidal power plants would lose most

108
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:46,820
of their energy.

109
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:49,700
And some coastlines would slowly reshape

110
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:50,300
themselves.

111
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,180
But the ocean is not the

112
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:53,740
only thing that follows the moon.

113
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,240
Many living things keep time by

114
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:56,560
it.

115
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,620
And without it,

116
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,000
their clocks stop.

117
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,380
Every year,

118
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,780
many corals release their eggs on

119
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:03,980
the same few nights.

120
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:06,660
Scientists think moonlight helps them pick

121
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,180
the timing.

122
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:08,420
Without it,

123
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,260
that timing could fall apart.

124
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,820
Some crabs time their spawning to

125
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:13,340
the tides.

126
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:15,700
Baby sea turtles hatch at night

127
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,520
and head for the brightest horizon.

128
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:19,760
Light over the water helps guide

129
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:20,560
them to the sea.

130
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:21,940
Without moonlight,

131
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:24,240
more might wander towards city lights

132
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:24,740
instead.

133
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,440
Even some tiny plankton move up

134
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,480
and down with the moon.

135
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:30,000
One missing moon,

136
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:31,860
and the whole web of life

137
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:32,520
feels it.

138
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:33,220
Now,

139
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,320
let's talk about something humans built

140
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,000
around the moon.

141
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:37,100
Our calendars.

142
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,480
The word month comes from the

143
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:39,660
moon.

144
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:41,360
For thousands of years,

145
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,660
people tracked time by its phases.

146
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:46,340
Many cultures still use lunar calendars

147
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:46,840
today.

148
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,100
Chinese New Year follows the moon.

149
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:51,040
So does the Mid -Autumn Festival,

150
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:52,980
the festival of the full moon.

151
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,420
Ramadan begins when the new crescent

152
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,240
moon is seen.

153
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:57,380
Without a moon,

154
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,580
these dates would need new rules.

155
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,720
Billions of people would have to

156
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:02,860
rethink their traditions.

157
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,500
And there would be no more

158
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,500
solar eclipses.

159
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:07,920
Never again would day turn to

160
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,940
night for a few minutes.

161
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,960
No more lunar eclipses either.

162
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,700
No more blood moons.

163
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,120
Thousands of years of stories,

164
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:15,920
songs,

165
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:18,000
and art would all be about

166
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,880
something that is no longer there.

167
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:20,620
Now,

168
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:22,160
let's bust some myths.

169
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,940
Would Earth fly out of its

170
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:24,240
orbit?

171
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:25,080
No.

172
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:26,740
Earth orbits the Sun,

173
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,600
and the moon is tiny in

174
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,100
comparison.

175
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:31,020
Our path around the Sun would

176
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:31,920
barely change.

177
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:34,080
Would you float away or feel

178
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:34,440
lighter?

179
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:35,560
Also no.

180
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,260
The moon's pull on you is

181
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:37,720
tiny.

182
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,060
You'd weigh almost exactly the same.

183
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:41,440
What about asteroids?

184
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,240
Does the moon protect us?

185
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:44,340
Not really.

186
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:46,560
It blocks only a tiny fraction

187
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,480
of space rocks.

188
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,680
So the sky wouldn't suddenly start

189
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,640
raining meteors.

190
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,200
The real danger is much slower

191
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,620
and much bigger.

192
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:55,660
But first,

193
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,260
think about space travel.

194
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,320
Twelve people have walked on the

195
00:04:59,320 --> 00:04:59,540
moon.

196
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:00,740
Their footprints,

197
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:01,540
flags,

198
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,680
and rovers would vanish with it.

199
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,640
Right now,

200
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:06,920
countries are planning to return and

201
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,040
even build bases.

202
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:10,080
All of those plans would be

203
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:10,940
gone overnight.

204
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:13,180
The moon is also our practice

205
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,500
ground for going to Mars.

206
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,680
Without it,

207
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:18,400
Mars suddenly feels much further away.

208
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:19,440
And now,

209
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:20,460
the slow,

210
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:21,660
bigger change.

211
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,340
Earth is tilted.

212
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,800
That tilt gives us our seasons.

213
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:26,980
Right now,

214
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:28,980
the tilt stays fairly steady.

215
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:31,380
Scientists think the moon helps keep

216
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:32,000
it that way.

217
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,040
Without it,

218
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,760
over millions of years,

219
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:37,160
the tilt could wobble much more.

220
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:39,300
A bigger tilt could mean much

221
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:40,340
harsher seasons,

222
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:41,860
scorching summers,

223
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:43,460
and brutal winters.

224
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,120
Climates could shift,

225
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,120
and some places might become hard

226
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:47,840
to live in.

227
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,980
This wouldn't happen in your lifetime.

228
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,660
It would take a very,

229
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,160
very long time.

230
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,940
The moon also slowly drags on

231
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:56,620
Earth's spin.

232
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,320
That's why our days have been

233
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:00,240
getting slightly longer for ages.

234
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,480
Without the moon,

235
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,600
that slowing would mostly stop.

236
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:04,460
So,

237
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:05,600
would we survive?

238
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:06,740
Yes,

239
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,680
but Earth would be a darker,

240
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:09,620
calmer,

241
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,000
stranger place.

242
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,600
And here's the twist.

243
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,760
The moon is already leaving.

244
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,240
It drifts away about 4 cm

245
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,280
every year,

246
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:20,120
about as fast as your fingernails

247
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:20,460
grow.

248
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,480
It won't leave us anytime soon,

249
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:24,200
but it keeps getting a little

250
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:24,700
further.

251
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:26,400
So next time you see it,

252
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:27,940
take a second to look up.

253
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,560
It does more for us than

254
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,720
you ever realized.

255
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,100
Follow for more what -ifs.

256
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,280
See you in the next one!

